{
  "inShort": "With no build or test notes shared, the checkpoint is behind on evidence. Five-player testing was reported, but what got done remains unknown because no playable work was shown. This evidence gap is common and can still be closed within this checkpoint.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd2l00k5kmz8u4ocak9l",
      "text": "The public repository of Godot demo projects matches the task. It provides reusable examples, not evidence of the game's islands, tides or co-op sailing."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd3300k6kmz8rs96hp7n",
      "text": "The animated reference video remains done. Inspection reached only the Big Buck Bunny title and thumbnail, so animation was not verified. Reusing that link in the sprint devlog does not show the game's chosen style."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd4500k7kmz8lmxh6bq4",
      "text": "The reference article on playtesting matches the task. It explains testing methods, but does not document the reported five-player sessions."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Where can the playable build, co-op instructions and five-player session notes be opened?",
    "Did those sessions cover both islands and two-player sailing, or only the tide loop?",
    "What did players' actions establish about the core mechanic?",
    "How much engineering time is available for the final week?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "“Devlog #3” reported five-player tide testing: 0 applause and 0 views. Its landscape photo and film thumbnail show no gameplay; no game link is listed.",
    "team": "Only 10–15 hours a week are stated, so total capacity remains uncertain. Mia has not confirmed work for two sprints, leaving engineering coverage for the playable slice unconfirmed.",
    "management": "With one week left, the completed reference tasks do not establish the playable slice. The published prototype devlog meets the sole formal stage requirement, but does not prove the core works or the style is chosen."
  }
}

